{
    "id": "getting-started/build-with-a-coding-agent",
    "title": "Build with a coding agent",
    "description": "What the Boost guideline, the firstlight-init and building-firstlight-screens skills, and llms.txt give your coding agent, and how to set them up.",
    "group": "Getting started",
    "anchors": {
        "build-with-a-coding-agent": "overview",
        "set-up-boost": "set-up-boost",
        "what-your-agent-gets": "what-your-agent-gets",
        "the-guidelines-rules": "what-your-agent-gets",
        "ask-for-an-app": "ask-for-an-app",
        "what-still-needs-a-person": "what-still-needs-a-person"
    },
    "chapters": {
        "overview": {
            "title": "Overview",
            "blocks": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "Firstlight is written to be built with by coding agents. The package ships a "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Laravel Boost",
                            "link": 0
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " guideline and two Boost skills, and its documentation is published as "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "llms.txt",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " and "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "llms-full.txt",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": ". Together they tell an agent which screens to build from which recipe, which control to use for each value, and which mistakes to avoid."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        "set-up-boost": {
            "title": "Set up Boost",
            "blocks": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "Install Firstlight as described in "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Installation",
                            "link": 1
                        },
                        {
                            "text": ", then add Laravel Boost to the application and run its installer:"
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "code",
                    "language": "bash",
                    "text": "composer require laravel/boost --dev\nphp artisan boost:install"
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "Boost finds the guideline and skills in Firstlight's "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "resources/boost",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " directory and writes them into your agent's files, such as "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "AGENTS.md",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": ", "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "CLAUDE.md",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": ", and its skills directory. If Boost is already installed, pick up Firstlight with:"
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "code",
                    "language": "bash",
                    "text": "php artisan boost:update --discover"
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "Run "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "php artisan boost:update",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " after each Firstlight update so the guideline and skills match the installed version."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        "what-your-agent-gets": {
            "title": "What your agent gets",
            "blocks": [
                {
                    "type": "definition",
                    "term": {
                        "text": "Guideline"
                    },
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "label": "When the agent reads it",
                            "text": "Always, as part of the agent's instructions"
                        },
                        {
                            "label": "What it contains",
                            "text": "The rules every Firstlight screen follows, the six recipes, the screen generator, and a tested example"
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "definition",
                    "term": {
                        "runs": [
                            {
                                "text": "firstlight-init",
                                "code": true
                            },
                            {
                                "text": " skill"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "label": "When the agent reads it",
                            "text": "When asked to start, set up, or scaffold a Firstlight app"
                        },
                        {
                            "label": "What it contains",
                            "text": "An interview about the app, a proposed layout, recipe screens and plugins, the app's name, ID, colours, icon and locale, and the confirmed screens with tests"
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "definition",
                    "term": {
                        "runs": [
                            {
                                "text": "building-firstlight-screens",
                                "code": true
                            },
                            {
                                "text": " skill"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "label": "When the agent reads it",
                            "text": "When adding or changing a screen, form, list, or settings page"
                        },
                        {
                            "label": "What it contains",
                            "text": "Which recipe to start from, which control fits each value, the workflow, and what never to do"
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "definition",
                    "term": {
                        "runs": [
                            {
                                "text": "llms.txt",
                                "link": 2,
                                "code": true
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "label": "When the agent reads it",
                            "text": "When the agent needs a page"
                        },
                        {
                            "label": "What it contains",
                            "text": "Every documentation page with a one-line summary"
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "definition",
                    "term": {
                        "runs": [
                            {
                                "text": "llms-full.txt",
                                "link": 3,
                                "code": true
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "label": "When the agent reads it",
                            "text": "When the agent needs the whole reference"
                        },
                        {
                            "label": "What it contains",
                            "text": "The full text of every documentation page in one file"
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "The package also includes "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "llms-full.txt",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " at "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "vendor/firstlightui/nativephp/llms-full.txt",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": ", so an agent can read the reference for the installed version without network access."
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "heading",
                    "text": "The guideline's rules"
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The guideline keeps an agent on the same path as the recipes:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "item",
                    "marker": "•",
                    "depth": 0,
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "Screens extend "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "FirstlightUI\\NativeComponent",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "."
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "item",
                    "marker": "•",
                    "depth": 0,
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "Controls are "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "<firstlight:*>",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " tags, with one Blade view for both platforms."
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "item",
                    "marker": "•",
                    "depth": 0,
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "Navigation chrome comes from NativePHP: layouts return "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "true",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " from "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "usesNativeChrome()",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": ". No custom-drawn tab bars, drawers, charts, or carousels."
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "item",
                    "marker": "•",
                    "depth": 0,
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "Validation is Laravel validation, with "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "$rules",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " or a Form Request passed to "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "$this->validate()",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": ". Fields show their own errors."
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "item",
                    "marker": "•",
                    "depth": 0,
                    "text": "Destructive actions open a Confirmation Dialog and authorize in PHP."
                },
                {
                    "type": "item",
                    "marker": "•",
                    "depth": 0,
                    "text": "Colours come from the NativePHP theme, not from markup."
                }
            ]
        },
        "ask-for-an-app": {
            "title": "Ask for an app",
            "blocks": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "With Boost installed, describe the app rather than the controls. "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Start a new app",
                            "link": 4
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " walks through the whole process. For example:"
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Start a Firstlight app for field technicians. They see the day's jobs, add photos and notes, and keep working without signal."
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "The "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "firstlight-init",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " skill asks what the app does, then proposes tabs or a single stack, a screen for each part of the app built from a "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "recipe",
                            "link": 5
                        },
                        {
                            "text": ", and the NativePHP plugins that fit. It then proposes the app name, app ID, brand colour, icon, splash, locale, and minimum OS, and you change any of them in your reply. It writes the plan to "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "firstlight-starter.json",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " and builds nothing until you confirm it. Then it runs:"
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "code",
                    "language": "bash",
                    "text": "php artisan firstlight:starter"
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "The command installs the plugins you accepted, sets the app's name, ID, colours, locale, timezone and permission text, and writes the native-chrome layout and each screen with its Pest test. It lists what is left for you in "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "STARTER.md",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": ", such as signing, store listings, and any screen it has no template for yet, which the agent then builds from its recipe. Running it again keeps files you have changed unless you pass "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "--force",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": ". You can also write the plan yourself, starting from "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "vendor/firstlightui/nativephp/resources/starter/firstlight-starter.example.json",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": ", and run the command without an agent."
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "The skill picks plugins from a list shipped with Firstlight at "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "vendor/firstlightui/nativephp/resources/starter/plugins.json",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": ", which says what each plugin does on iOS and Android and which Firstlight features make a plugin unnecessary. Free plugins are included when the app needs them. Paid plugins are only offered, marked as paid, and installed only when you say yes; NativePHP serves them only to an account that has bought them, so buy one before you accept it, or the skill builds the app without it and leaves you the steps to add it. Community plugins come with a notice that neither Firstlight nor NativePHP maintains or warrants them."
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "For later screens, ask for the outcome, such as \"add a screen to edit a job\". The "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "building-firstlight-screens",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " skill picks the matching recipe, or starts from the generator:"
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "code",
                    "language": "bash",
                    "text": "php artisan make:firstlight-screen EditJob --form --test"
                }
            ]
        },
        "what-still-needs-a-person": {
            "title": "What still needs a person",
            "blocks": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "An agent can write screens and run their Pest tests. It cannot see the app on a device. Both skills end by asking you to run the app on an iOS simulator and an Android emulator and check navigation, field errors, and deletion on both. Check accessibility too. See "
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Accessibility",
                            "link": 6
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " for what Firstlight covers and what your app still owns."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    },
